# Fault f_vlaw (writer 6): f's rule `base v v1` was refused LOAD-LAWDATE although v1 governs always. L §4.3 rule 1:
# law-dated is "an input, band, def or rule whose value can change with the law date: one with a row or version whose
# span isn't `always`"; rule 2: "if it reads nothing law-dated, it needs no law date". v1 governs always, and n's row
# governs always, so neither f nor g states `at`: q = (4 + 1, 4 + 1) = (5, 5).
=== f_vlaw.tally
model fvlaw
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

input n: int

def f: int
  rule base v v1 = n + 1

def g: int = n + 1

ask q: f, g

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n = 4 "row"
=== expect
q: (5, 5)
  cut 2026-10-25
